# setup.py names the core's .cpp files as sources, so sdist picks those up on
# its own. The headers it does not, and without them the sdist cannot compile:
# `pip install pace-spatial` would fail at the first #include. The manifest is
# what makes a source install work at all.
include LICENSE
include README.md
include src/core/*.hpp
include src/core_manifest.json
include pace/py.typed

# The test fixtures are R's own fits and run to megabytes. Tests run from a
# git checkout, where CI runs them; shipping them in every sdist is weight
# nobody installing the package needs.
prune tests
prune examples
prune tools
